Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Friction compensation and integrator as parameters
 (defaults unchanged)

- integrator_weights / integrator_limits replace the hard-coded integral
  weights and anti-windup clamps (same defaults).
- friction_compensation: none (default) | lugre | coulomb | velocity
  - lugre: the upstream calculate_tau_friction(), now scaled with dt (was
    fixed to 1 kHz), optional |error| threshold (upstream zeroes all
    negative errors), optional offsets; added before the torque-rate limit.
  - coulomb: identified Coulomb friction in the direction of the impedance
    torque + viscous on measured velocity.
  - velocity: identified Coulomb (tanh on joint velocity) + viscous; zero
    at rest, so the stiffness stays as set.
- Fix: a local tau_impedance shadowed the member that the friction code reads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
