From e6d5f8de57c0f76457c60dd36a908dd26270758d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nils Johnson <njohnson@ethz.ch>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:23:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] MPC tracking interface (ci_mpc_msgs/MpcCommand)

- Subscribes /cartesian_impedance_controller/mpc_command through a realtime
  buffer. The newest command sets the pose directly (no reference filter),
  the desired twist (damping now on the velocity error), a feedforward wrench,
  optional diagonal K / D and integral gating (decays at mpc_integral_off_leak).
- Without a new command for mpc_timeout (default 50 ms, counted in control
  cycles) it holds the current pose, drops twist/feedforward and resets the
  integral. reference_pose keeps working as before.
- Sim (no friction): circle r 5 cm / 5 s RMS 0.65 mm (reference_pose path:
  33 mm), feedforward cancels a 10 N push (-0.01 mm), commanded K 500 ->
  9.97 mm under 5 N, integral gating 0.01 vs 2.39 mm, timeout drift 0.04 mm.
- Depends on ci_mpc_msgs (ci_mpc repo) and realtime_tools.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
